{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And in the year</b> — The book says that it is the second year of Nebuchadnezzar's reign over Jerusalem after Zedekiah rebelled against him and he destroyed it. And R. Moses said: for two years remained of his reign. And we have not found anything like this in all of Scripture. And what seems correct to me: [it refers to] his reign over all the nations whom Jeremiah mentioned he would conquer; then he was at rest and thought thoughts upon his bed concerning what would be at the end of days, as Daniel mentioned. And he mentioned 'dreams' because in the image there is gold and silver and bronze and iron and pottery, and the way of a dreamer is to see one thing." "<b>And was troubled</b> — Like נפעמתי ולא אדבר, and [like] וגזרתם את הולם פעם, as a person who is dazed and bewildered. The Gaon [Saadia] said: For Pharaoh knew the dream but did not know its interpretation; therefore concerning Pharaoh it is written ותפעם רוחו, which is in the nifal conjugation. And Nebuchadnezzar, who did not know the dream or the interpretation, it is written about him ותתפעם רוחו. If so, what shall one do, for he [David] says ותפעם רוחי?! It is possible that the dagesh in the peh [of ותפעם] stands in place of the nun of the nifal, for the active verb is nifal, like וילחם בישראל — or the dagesh in the peh is for the assimilation of the tav of the hitpa'el, and then ותפעם רוחו would be like 'his strength was agitated' — in the manner of וכבס המטהר את בגדיו, and the meaning is that restlessness came upon him, as in שנתי ערבה לי in the sense of שבוש, and like it נהייתי ונחליתי, and it is close in meaning to נהי נהיה."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "The last sentence is textually difficult and possibly corrupt; rendered hyper-literally. The citation שנתי ערבה לי (Psalms 6:7) is rendered in the sense Ibn Ezra proposes, reading ערבה as 'was pleasant' reshaped to mean restlessness, and שבוש read as 'confusion' from the root שוב; both readings are uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:07.938694734Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}